lesson: 136
title: Perimeter: all the way round a triangle
level: primary-2
stars: 1
explain: The perimeter of a shape is the length all the way round it: add the lengths of all its sides.
explain: A triangle has 3 sides. If one side is 5 cm and each of the other two is 3 cm longer, they are 8 cm each.
explain: Then the perimeter is 5 + 8 + 8 = 21 cm.
vars: a=name x=3..20 d=2..9
answer: 3 * x + 2 * d
exercise: A triangle has one side of {x} cm. Each of the other two sides is {d} cm longer. What is the perimeter of the triangle?
exercise: {a} bends a wire into a triangle. One side is {x} cm, the other two sides are {x+d} cm each. How long is the wire?
exercise: Two sides of a triangle are {x+d} cm each, and the third is {d} cm shorter. Find the perimeter.
exercise: A triangular flower bed has sides of {x} m, {x+d} m and {x+d} m. How many metres of fence go round it?
exercise: The shortest side of a triangle is {x} cm. The other two sides are equal, and each is {d} cm longer than the shortest. What is the perimeter?
test: What length of ribbon goes once round a triangle with sides {x+d} cm, {x} cm and {x+d} cm?
test: A triangle's two equal sides are {x+d} cm long and its third side is {d} cm shorter than them. How many centimetres is it all the way round?
test: {a} walks once round a triangular field. One side is {x} m long; the other two are both {d} m longer. How many metres does {a.he} walk?
exercise: What is the perimeter of a triangle whose shortest side is {x} cm and whose other two sides are each {d} cm longer?
exercise: Sides: {x} cm, {x+d} cm, {x+d} cm. Perimeter?
exercise: A triangular garden in Kent has one side of {x} m and two equal sides of {x+d} m. How many metres is it all the way round?
exercise: {a} draws a triangle with sides of {x+d} cm, {x+d} cm and {x} cm. What is the perimeter?
exercise: The base of a triangle is {x} cm, and both other sides are {d} cm longer than the base. Add up the sides to find the perimeter.
exercise: A triangular sail in Nova Scotia has two edges of {x+d} m each and a third edge {d} m shorter. What is the total length of its edges?
exercise: {a} makes a triangle from three sticks: one is {x} cm, and each of the others is {d} cm longer. How many centimetres of stick does {a.he} use?
exercise: A triangle has one side of {x} m and two sides of {x+d} m each. How many metres is its perimeter?
test: A triangular park in Oregon has a short side of {x} m; the two long sides are equal and {d} m longer than it. How far is one lap round the park?
test: How much lace edges a triangular flag with one side {x} cm and the two other sides {x+d} cm each?
test: Two equal sides of {x+d} cm and one side of {x} cm: find the distance round this triangle.
test: {a} runs once round a triangular track in Adelaide. Its sides are {x+d} m, {x} m and {x+d} m. How many metres is the lap?
test: The equal sides of a triangle are {d} cm longer than its shortest side, which is {x} cm. Give the total of all three sides.
test: A farmer in Wexford puts a fence round a triangular pen. One side is {x} m, and the other two each exceed it by {d} m. How long is the fence?
exercise: triangle, one side {x} cm, other two {d} cm longer each. perimeter?
exercise: {a} bent a wire into a triangle, sides {x} cm, {x+d} cm and {x+d+1} — no wait, {x+d} cm. how long's the wire
exercise: my sister says sides {x}, {x+d}, {x+d} cm make {x+2*d} cm all round. nah, whats the real perimeter
exercise: {a} drew a triangle in 5 minutes lol, one side {x} cm, the other two sides {x+d} cm each. how far round it
test: two sides {x+d} cm each, third one's {d} cm shorter. all the way round?
test: triangle: {x} cm, {x+d} cm, {x+d} cm. perimeter pls
test: {a} says a triangle with {x} cm and two sides {d} cm longer is {3*x+d} cm round. wrong yeah? whats it really
exam: It is given that one side of a triangle measures {x} cm and that each of the remaining two sides exceeds it by {d} cm. Determine the perimeter of the triangle in centimetres.
exam: Whereas {a} fashions a wire into a triangle having one side of {x} cm and two sides of {x+d} cm each, ascertain the total length of the wire.
exam: Two sides of a triangle measure {x+d} cm each, the third being {d} cm shorter than either. State the perimeter in centimetres.
exam: Compute the sum of the side lengths of a triangle whose sides are {x} cm, {x+d} cm and {x+d} cm.
exercise: {a} was economical with the truth: {a.he} said every side of {a.his} triangle was {x} cm, but really one side is {x} cm and the other two are {x+d} cm each. What is the real perimeter?
exercise: Grandad passed away and left {a} his triangular vegetable patch. One side is {x} m, and each of the other two is {d} m longer. How many metres of new fence go all the way round it?
test: the old fence round the goat pen finally carked it, bloody thing. pen's a triangle: {x} m, {x+d} m, {x+d} m. how much new fence we buying, genius?
